  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nModels are still showing the first real Pacific cold front of the \nseason moving into TX, but the timing is not consistent. Now it's \nlooking later in the week. Despite this change there are still \nchances for widespread rain starting Tuesday. Now models are showing \nrain chances extending into Saturday. They are also showing signs of \npossible heavy area at times during this period. Although our \nconfidence for the timing is low, currently the best chances for \nheavy rain are Wednesday night through Thursday night. The airmass \nchange is looking less significant, but all the clouds and rain will \nlikely keep daytime temperatures down during the second half of the \nweek, and highs should stay in the 80s Thursday through Saturday.",
